&Q000794 = The heron and the turtle
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.5.9.2
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.5.9.2&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div segment A

A.1. [ŋiš-gi] a-na gu₃# [mu-un-de₂ mu₂]-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ŋešgi[thicket]; ana[what?]; gu[voice]; de[pour]; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#tr.en: What do they say in the reedbeds whose growth is good? In the wide reedbeds of @wSN{Tutub}, whose growth is good? In the marshes of @wSN{Kiritaba}, whose growth is good? In the @fsux{adara} thickets of @wSN{Akšak}, whose growth is good? In @wDN{Enki's} interconnecting (?) lagoons, whose growth is good? In the smaller lagoon, @wDN{Enki's} lagoon, whose growth is good? In @wDN{Enki's} @fsux{barbar} reeds, whose growth is good? In the little @fsux{zi} reeds of @wSN{Urim}, whose growth is good? In @wSN{Urim}, where cows and calves abound, whose growth is good? 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 30; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 53

A.2. [ŋiš-gi] daŋal# tu-tu-[ub-ba]{[ki]}-[a-ka] mu₂-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ŋešgi[thicket]; daŋal[wide]; Tutub[1]SN; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. [ambar-ra kiri₈]-tab-ba{ki}-a-[ka] mu₂-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ambar[reed-bed]; Kiritaba[1]SN; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. [a-dar]-ra akšak{ki}-a-ka mu₂-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: adar[plant]; Akšak[1]SN; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

