#lem: barbar[reed]; Enkik[1]DN; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. urim₂{ki}-ma gi-zi di₄-di₄-la₂ mu₂-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: Urim[1]SN; gizi[fresh reed]; didila[small(er)]; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. urim₂{ki}-ma ab₂ lu amar lu-a re mu₂-a-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: Urim[1]SN; ab[cow]; lu[abundant]; amar[calf]; lu[abundant]; re[that]; mu[grow]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. ud-bi-a a# X gi#-ta nam-kud amaš-e pa nam-e₃
#lem: ud[sun]; a[water]; X; gi[reed]; kud[cut]; amaš[sheepfold]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: At that time, the water was drained away from the reeds ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. {u₂}aš-tal₂-tal₂ ŋiš-gi-ta numun-bi sal-sal-e
#lem: aštaltal[plant]; ŋešgi[thicket]; numun[seed]; sal[thin]
#tr.en: and they were visible at the sheepfold. The @fsux{aštaltal} plant, spreading its seeds from the reedbeds, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. {u₂}ku-mul tur-tur ki-ta nam-ta-an-e₃ nam-di₄-di₄-la₂ dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: gamun[cumin]; tur[small]; ki[place]; e[leave]; namdidila[smallness]; dug[good]
#tr.en: and the little @fsux{kumul} plants came out of the earth: they are good as little ones. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. {gi}en₃-bar tur-re suh₁₀ nam-dub-dub nam-ki-sikil dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: enbar[reed]; tur[small]; suh[crown]; dub[heap up]; namkisikil[status as a young woman]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The small @fsux{enbar} reed tighten her headdress: it is good as a young maiden. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. {gi}ub-zal iri-bi-da nam-da-DI nam-ŋuruš dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ubzal[young reeds]; iri[city]; X; namŋuruš[manliness]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The @fsux{ubzal} reed goes about the city: it is good as a young man. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. {gi}pe-el-la₂ ur₂-ra saŋ-še₃ nam-ib-dul e₂-gi₄-a dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: pela[reed]; ur[root]; saŋ[head]; dul[cover]; egia[bride]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The @fsux{pela} reed is covered from bottom to top: it is a good daughter-in-law. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. {gi}pe-el-la₂ ur₂-ra saŋ-še₃ nam-ta-ab-gi₄ dumu ban₃-da dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: pela[reed]; ur[root]; saŋ[head]; gi[turn]; dumu[child]; banda[junior]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The @fsux{pela} reed turns from bottom to top: it is a good young son. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. {gi}gašam-e ki am₃-burudₓ(U)-e nam-ab-ba dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: gašam[reed]; ki[place]; burud[perforate]; namabba[old age]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The @fsux{gašam} reed digs in the ground: it is good as an old man. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. gi-zi ni₂-bi-a nam-mu-un-šu₂ nam-um-ma dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: gizi[fresh reed]; ni[self]; šuš[cover]; namumma[agedness]; dug[good]
#tr.en: The @fsux{zi} reed …… on its own: it is good as an old woman. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. [ŋiš]-gi# sig₇-ga-bi saŋ nam-il₂ gu₃-de₂-a dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ŋešgi[thicket]; sissig[green-yellow]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; Gudea[1]RN; dug[good]
#tr.en: The reedbed lifts its head beautifully: it is a good @wRN{Gudea}. The @fsux{ildag} tree lifts its head in the irrigation ditch: 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. {ŋiš}ildag₂ šita₃-na saŋ nam-il₂ nam-lugal-la dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: ildag[poplar]; šitan[water-channel]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; namlugal[kingship]; dug[good]
#tr.en: it is good as a king. …… with bright branches: 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. [...]-e pa mul-mul-la dumu lugal-la dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: X; pa[branch]; mul[shine]; dumu[child]; lugal[king]; dug[good]
#tr.en: it is a good prince. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. [ud-bi]-a zag ŋiš-gi-e ki-a tuš-e u₃-gul mu-na-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#lem: ud[sun]; zag[side]; ŋešgi[thicket]; ki[place]; tuš[sit (down)]; ugul[cvne]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: On that day, beside the reedbeds, someone sitting on the bank prays: @q[turtle,]{“Let me snatch away the heron's eggs, let me take them away ……, so that the gift-bringing bird will not be able to make a gift, so that the gift-bringing heron will not be able make a gift!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

